Z||000005||86SE||07-08-2000||01:46 AM||||I just thought of this, just mabey with a little bit of engineering it might work.  If you take a small portable air compressor (1.5-2 cubic feet of uncompressed room) and fill it to about 80-100psi and run a hose from the compressor to the intake just before the throttle body.  Then rig up a solenoid that will allow the air to flow into the plenium by the press of a button?!?!  will this work?  it seems a little far fetched.......<P>Just for quick boosts - If you have an air compressor, refilling would be a snap.  But I dont know how much boost a small compressor would create with 50-100 psi in it....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>Hmmmmm, possibliy it will work....any input?<BR>It would be a HELL of a thing if it created 5 psi boost!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Fiero<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 86SE (edited 07-08-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000006||olympic||07-08-2000||05:46 AM||||  Here's another link <A HREF="http://www.turbo-zet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.turbo-zet.com</A>   I don't think these things are worth the money and effort.  It would probably be cheaper to add a 40-50 hp shot of nitrous and your gains would be alot greater.  Remember, it takes power to make boost.  A supercharger will draw many hp to make 7 psi.  1 hp=750 watts.  These electric sc's claim to use only 200 watts or so.<P>------------------<BR>"Born free....taxed to death."||||reg||1
